    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class in the project, and it passes. The build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the immutable structured `OWNER_CREATED` audit event.\n\n**New file \u2014 `rest/audit/OwnerCreatedEvent.java`:** an immutable `record` carrying `{seq, ownerId, customerCode, membershipLevel, event}`. Field order matches the spec's JSON, `event` is fixed to `\"OWNER_CREATED\"`, and `toJson()` serializes it via Jackson to a compact JSON object.\n\n**`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`:**\n- Added a static `AtomicLong AUDIT_SEQUENCE` so `seq` increases monotonically across every create, independent of owner id.\n- After the existing human-readable audit line, `addOwner` now calls `emitOwnerCreatedEvent(owner)`, which stamps the next sequence number and logs the JSON event to the `AUDIT` logger.\n- The event's identifier value comes from a single seam, `primaryIdentifier(owner)`, which today returns `owner.getCustomerCode()`. This is the designed extension point: when the customer code is later unified into the member id, only that one accessor changes and the event automatically carries the member id instead \u2014 satisfying the \"current primary identifier\" requirement.\n\nEmitted output confirms both lines are present:\n```\nINFO  AUDIT - owner created id=11 customerCode=NSW-16E6609E ...\nINFO  AUDIT - {\"seq\":1,\"ownerId\":11,\"customerCode\":\"NSW-16E6609E\",\"membershipLevel\":1,\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}\n```\n\nThe full test suite (`AcceptanceTest`) passes: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
